From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 18:05:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 71/74] media: qcom: camss: correct the C-PHY configuration
 against a live dump

With the first C-PHY attempt the link trained and full-width lines
arrived, but every frame stopped after exactly 768 of its 2256 lines,
and the receiver logged EOT reception errors and lane FIFO overflows.

The vendor driver has a csiphy_dump module parameter, so compare against
the truth: dump the whole PHY register space on the vendor kernel while
it streams this camera, and diff against what this driver programs. That
found three wrong values and a set of missing writes -- and showed that
the kernel the device ships does not match its own published source, so
the dump is what the hardware demonstrably works with:

 - the common mode word CTRL7 is 0x52, not the 0x02 the D-PHY path uses
 - the trio mask is mirrored into CTRL55, and two more common words are
   set that the D-PHY path never touches
 - one word per trio differs from the published table (0xac, not 0xa0)
 - six static words per trio are missing from the published table
   entirely, among them what looks like the calibration kick that lets
   the PHY trim each wire pair
 - the settle count is 0x1d; the D-PHY formula computes for a signalling
   scheme this link does not use

The per-wire trim values themselves are deliberately not copied: they
differ wire to wire on the same device, which marks them as calibration
results rather than configuration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
